WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.000
-Well, it's 2022,
and believe it or not,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.934
all of our problems are solved,

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.267
the pandemic is over
and our democracy is saved.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.133
Wait, I'm sorry. Hold on.
That doesn't sound right.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.567
-See, I told you.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.534
Seth, I bet Bryan 100 bucks

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.901
that you read anything
I put in the cards.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.300
Pay up, Bry.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.434
-Damn it, Wally.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.000
If you ever pull anything
like that again,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.868
I'll give you a raise
and buy you a car!

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.868
What?
-Hoo-ho!

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:28.868
Yes!
I did it again.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.067
-Can I just have
the real cards now, Wally?!

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.634
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.634
COVID is more widespread
than ever,

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.167
and our democracy
is on the brink.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.801
Yes, that is more like it.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.834
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.133
♪♪

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:49.934
One of the biggest mistakes
we as human beings make

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:53.434
is thinking next year
will be better than last year,

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.667
even though the best indicator
of how things are going to go

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.367
is how they've been going.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.133
It's not like Father Time
pulls Baby New Year aside

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:02.334
and says,
"Go easy on him, kid,

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:05.033
because I was a real ass ache.

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.901
Remember when 2020 ended
and we all thought

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.367
we were in the clear,
only to make it six days

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.701
until the Capitol storm?

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.133
And if you thought
that was crazy,

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.701
we only made it two days
into 2022

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.734
before the worst thing
at a Jets game

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.767
was somehow
not Jets related.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.467
And I have to say this year's
New Year celebrations

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.868
did not inspire a lot
of confidence that 2022

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:27.734
is going to be
a much more cheerful year.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.100
For example,
at one point they played

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.934
John Lennon's "Imagine"
per tradition

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:34.267
while a smaller-than-usual
crowd danced in giant

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:37.100
hats branded with the Planet
Fitness logo.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.634
-♪ Imagine no possessions ♪

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.634
-Now, in fairness
to those people,

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.200
the Beatles were wearing
those same hats

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.601
in the "Get Back" documentary.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.200
Who can forget
that incredible moment

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.734
when John turned to Paul
and said,

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:54.067
"Hey, Paul, wouldn't it be great
if there was peace on Earth

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.767
and a gym
with no enrollment fees?"

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.267
"Well, that would be Super,
John."

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.367
"And what are they gave you
the first month free?"

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:03.400
"Oh, now you're giving me
the giggly wigglys, John.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.767
[ Siren blaring ]

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.634
Whoa, you know
what that siren means.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:07.834
New impression alert.

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:10.901
I spent the holiday break
at a special two-week

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:12.334
impression camp seminar

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.400
where we learned how to do
what's called a two-hander,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.033
where you impersonate
two people at once.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.767
It's like they say
at Impression camp,

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.434
"Do you want to be
life of the party

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.300
or would you rather go
to impression camp?"

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.834
Point is, I didn't know
him personally,

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:26.968
but I'm fairly confident
that is not what

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:30.367
John Lennon wanted us to imagine
when he wrote the song.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.400
Otherwise, the lyrics would
have been a little different.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.000
♪ Imagine there's a planet ♪

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.367
♪ Where you can exercise ♪

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:41.934
♪ Everybody's into fitness ♪

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.300
♪ They're are beefy guys ♪

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.400
I feel like by doing that,
it's like a favor to Gal Gadot.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.834
And by the way, if that
bizarre scene didn't give you

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.901
a sense of how we're entering
2022,

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:55.701
then how about this drunken rant
from CNN New Year's Eve co-host

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:59.234
Andy Cohen, who absolutely
went off on former Mayor

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.100
Bill de Blasio
after the ball dropped?

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.701
I don't know what
Andy's specific complaint is,

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.734
but it doesn't matter
because this is pretty much

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.467
how New Yorkers
talk about every mayor,

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:10.033
regardless of who they are
or what they do.

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.334
-Let me tell you something.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.434
-Please tell us something, Andy.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:17.467
-Watching Mayor de Blasio...

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:20.868
-Don't go on a rant.
-...do his "victory"

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:25.067
lap dance after four years...
-Don't -- don't do it.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:30.133
-...of the crappiest term
as the mayor of New York.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:32.033
-That's how you want
to start the new year?

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:35.133
-The only thing the Democrats
and Republicans can agree on

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:39.367
is what a horrible mayor
he has been.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:43.334
So sayonara, sucka.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:46.968
2022, It's a new year.

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.834
Because guess what?

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.300
I have a feeling of
I'm going to be standing

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.133
right here next year.

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.667
And you know
I'm not going to be looking at

00:03:55.667 --> 00:04:01.300
dancing as the city
comes apart.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.334
...you!

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.200
-I mean, I think he's been

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.801
spending too much time
with those "Real Housewives."

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:11.601
Even Jennifer would be like
you should have a club soda.

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:12.868
I mean, look at him.

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:15.334
Anderson Cooper is holding
him back by the jacket

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.467
the way you hold back
your friend

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.467
who is over served at SantaCon.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.467
Look, forget it, Chase.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:25.000
Let's just go harass
some outdoor diners.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.667
Given the choice
between those two,

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:30.667
I just want you to know you want
Andy to be the belligerent one.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:33.167
Because when Anderson Cooper
wants to fight you,

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.234
you're already dead.

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:36.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:39.200
And as for the rant itself,
agree or disagree,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.801
but if you've ever been
on the F train

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:42.767
or in a bar at 3:00 A.M.,
you've probably heard

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:45.100
that exact thing, word for word.
It's nothing personal.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.067
It's just a bargain
you make as mayor of this city.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.400
In return for getting
to live in a mansion,

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.167
you serve as a sponge
for everyone's rage.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.567
It's the only way we can live
together in this city.

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:55.968
We have to have a common enemy

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:58.133
in the form of the mayor,
whoever they are.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.100
Otherwise, we turn on each other
in the streets

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.968
and you'd see Spider-Man
and Buzz Lightyear

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.033
just wailing on each other
in Times Square while a cabbie

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:08.367
runs over the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.467
The same was true
for Bloomberg and Rudy.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.501
It'll be true for
Eric Adams as well.

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:13.701
Angry rants against the mayor

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.267
is such a standard part
of New York life

00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:17.501
they've been incorporated
into the subway announcements.

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:21.400
-Stand clear of the
closing doors, please.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:26.667
And remember freaking de Blasio
can kiss my ass.

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.434
Oh.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.300
Next stop, 42nd Street.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.534
-Yeah.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.067
So that kind of gives you
a good sense

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.100
of the state of things
as we enter 2022.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.567
That's not to say there
aren't reasons for optimism,

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:38.968
or at least reasons for us

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:41.267
all to be motivated to work
together toward a better future.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.367
We can't give in
to the fatalism,

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.934
and we have to keep pushing
forward together in solidarity

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:48.100
for a more just
and brighter world.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.934
But along the way,
we're going to do some shots

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:51.934
and they're going to be times
where we need Anderson Cooper

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.601
to hold us back.

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:55.501
So just, you know,
where your puffiest coat

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:58.834
because it's easier for him
to get a grip on it.

00:05:58.834 --> 00:06:01.033
For example, that Andy Cohen
New Year's Energy

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:02.834
is pretty much how I felt
when Florida Senator

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:06.133
Marco Rubio flippantly dismissed
the most recent COVID surge,

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:08.801
which is setting new records
for daily case numbers

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.501
and fueling rising
hospital admissions.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:13.534
On New Year's Eve,
Rubio tweeted, "Record numbers

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:15.334
testing positive
for a sore throat

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:17.367
isn't a crisis,
and people in the hospital

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:20.133
for car accidents
testing positive isn't surge.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:22.801
The real crisis
is the irrational hysteria,

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:24.534
which has people
with no symptoms

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:27.567
waiting hours for a test
or missing work for 10 days."

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:29.033
Irrational hysteria?

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.968
Anderson hold me back!

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:34.834
First of all,
you haunted ventriloquist dummy,

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:38.267
It's only a sore throat,
that's likely

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:40.300
because you're boosted
or at the very least,

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.167
double vaccinated,
which would be a far better

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.133
message for you to be pushing,

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:47.300
especially since you got
your shot before most Americans

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.767
even had access to the vaccine.

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:50.501
Do you remember that,
or did you block it out

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:52.501
because you were, you know,
being so hysterical?

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:56.000
Also, you think missing work
for 10 days is the real crisis

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.400
instead of letting people
stay home

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.234
to take care of themselves
and slow the spread?

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:01.434
That's pretty rich
coming from a senator

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.534
who once had one of the worst
attendance records in Congress.

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:07.067
And it's the true fact.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:09.467
One of the few true facts
I learned,

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:11.634
from of all people,
Donald Trump who brought it up

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:15.033
in a GOP primary debate
amid a chorus of boos.

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:18.367
-This guy number one --

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:22.067
the number one absentee record
in the United States.

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.834
He doesn't show up to vote.

00:07:24.834 --> 00:07:28.300
-Just a reminder, the guy
getting booed became president,

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.234
and those were Republicans
booing him.

00:07:32.234 --> 00:07:34.400
Also, you know it's bad
when Donald Trump of all people

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.934
slams you
for not working enough.

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:38.601
The guy spends most of his time
wandering around his Palm Beach

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:42.400
golf course like the ghost
of Haggard Vance.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.968
By the way
that clip is a reminder

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:46.501
if you ever want dirt
on any major Republican,

00:07:46.501 --> 00:07:49.100
you can just rewatch
the 2016 debates.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.133
Trump went through those guys
like Don Rickles

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:53.200
at the Copacabana.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.467
Rubio's attendance record
was so bad,

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:57.300
Trump didn't even have
to lie about it.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:00.067
Trump lies about everything,
even stuff that's good for him.

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:01.868
If he won the Nobel Prize,
he'd tell everyone

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:05.701
it was their best golfer,
big penis category.

00:08:05.701 --> 00:08:07.200
Can you imagine the conversation

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.634
with his staff
when Trump found out

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:10.133
he didn't have
to make something up?

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.234
"I'm going to lie and say
it doesn't show up to vote."

00:08:12.234 --> 00:08:14.133
"Well, it's not a lie, sir.
It's true."

00:08:14.133 --> 00:08:15.434
"Okay, well,
then I'm going to lie

00:08:15.434 --> 00:08:18.434
and say his real name
is Marcus Rubiokoski."

00:08:18.434 --> 00:08:20.400
"Well, what if, sir,
and this is just a suggestion,

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.267
what if you didn't lie
at all this time?"

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:23.367
"No, can do.

00:08:23.367 --> 00:08:25.334
I have to lie once
every five minutes

00:08:25.334 --> 00:08:27.367
or my brain explodes like
the buss from 'Speed'.

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:30.667
'Speed,' we love 'Speed,'
don't we, folks?

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:34.968
A young -- a young Sandy Bullock
and a breakthrough role.

00:08:34.968 --> 00:08:37.133
But I can't watch it anymore.

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:38.801
I can't watch
the film 'Speed' anymore.

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:40.834
It's very sad.
It's bad.

00:08:40.834 --> 00:08:42.834
I can't watch it anymore
because it reminds me

00:08:42.834 --> 00:08:47.000
of the 'Access Hollywood' bus
where I was treated very --

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.300
I was treated very unfairly,
very unfairly on this.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.067
But do you guys remember that?

00:08:52.067 --> 00:08:53.334
You barely do, don't you?

00:08:53.334 --> 00:08:56.367
Like the whole thing
was a dream.

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:57.534
But it's true.

00:08:57.534 --> 00:09:00.667
It's one of the many true
things that I did,

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:02.467
and everybody forgave me
and I became president."

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:04.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.534
I hope this is a reminder
that Republicans like Rubio

00:09:06.534 --> 00:09:08.334
pretend to be normal statesman
above the fray

00:09:08.334 --> 00:09:10.434
are arguably just as reckless
and unhinged

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:13.467
as the far right weirdos
like Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:09:13.467 --> 00:09:15.300
who has repeatedly
lied about the vaccines

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.701
and who recently called
for a "national divorce,"

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:20.033
which is, I guess,
the sequel to "National Velvet."

00:09:20.033 --> 00:09:23.634
How -- how would a national
divorce even work?

00:09:23.634 --> 00:09:26.334
Who would get the White House?
Who would pay alimony?

00:09:26.334 --> 00:09:27.801
Who would get custody of Eric?

00:09:27.801 --> 00:09:30.467
It would probably just be
the two sides

00:09:30.467 --> 00:09:31.734
pushing him back and forth.

00:09:31.734 --> 00:09:34.067
He's a Republican,
so he should go with you.

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:37.367
But he's a New Yorker,
so he should go with you.

00:09:37.367 --> 00:09:38.734
And then one critic said
it sounded like

00:09:38.734 --> 00:09:41.501
she was calling for a civil war,
Greene defended the tweet

00:09:41.501 --> 00:09:43.534
by writing that
"Divorces happen in court

00:09:43.534 --> 00:09:46.901
or perhaps for a country
can happen in Congress.

00:09:46.901 --> 00:09:48.968
Happy marriages are the result
of two committed people

00:09:48.968 --> 00:09:50.467
working together,
resolving differences

00:09:50.467 --> 00:09:52.100
and changing behavior
that hurts the other."

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:55.033
And by the way, this person
who said happy marriages

00:09:55.033 --> 00:09:58.167
required two sides to compromise
is also the same person

00:09:58.167 --> 00:10:00.534
who tweeted a truly depraved lie
about Democrats

00:10:00.534 --> 00:10:01.901
and COVID last week
when she said

00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:05.133
"The vaccines are failing
and the Democrats are tyrants.

00:10:05.133 --> 00:10:06.567
The entire effort
should be focused

00:10:06.567 --> 00:10:09.033
on life saving treatments
and returning life to normal.

00:10:09.033 --> 00:10:11.868
Wide open, no mask, no mandates,
no discrimination,

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:13.934
and lifesaving treatments
widely available."

00:10:13.934 --> 00:10:15.567
We all want
to get back to normal.

00:10:15.567 --> 00:10:17.467
You are the ones
who want to live

00:10:17.467 --> 00:10:19.334
with this endless cycle
of misery and death

00:10:19.334 --> 00:10:21.667
and just let a highly
contagious respiratory virus

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:23.434
ravaged the country.
That's not normal.

00:10:23.434 --> 00:10:25.834
The rest of us just want
to slow the spread of COVID

00:10:25.834 --> 00:10:28.100
and get back to something
that's actually normal.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.834
You know how badly I love
to go back to my old life

00:10:30.834 --> 00:10:34.067
of eating indoors at restaurants
without a mask on so the waiters

00:10:34.067 --> 00:10:36.033
would recognize my face
and comp my mail?

00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:37.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:37.834 --> 00:10:39.601
They always said
the same thing.

00:10:39.601 --> 00:10:41.667
"Oh, my God.
I loved you in 'The Office.'"

00:10:41.667 --> 00:10:43.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.234 --> 00:10:44.834
Hey, whatever.

00:10:44.834 --> 00:10:46.434
Whatever!

00:10:46.434 --> 00:10:51.033
Free cheesecake
is free cheesecake.

00:10:51.033 --> 00:10:52.601
Well, not surprisingly,
after all that,

00:10:52.601 --> 00:10:55.400
Greene's personal account
finally got kicked off Twitter.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.834
-Twitter is permanently
suspending the personal account

00:10:57.834 --> 00:11:00.267
of Representative
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:11:00.267 --> 00:11:01.968
According to
the social media company,

00:11:01.968 --> 00:11:04.834
it's because Greene repeatedly
posted false information

00:11:04.834 --> 00:11:06.200
about COVID-19.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.400
-The Georgia Republican
just releasing a statement

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.501
bashing the social media site,
writing,

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:13.968
"Twitter is an enemy to America
and can't handle the truth."

00:11:13.968 --> 00:11:16.267
-Oh, it looks like you finally
got that divorce you wanted.

00:11:16.267 --> 00:11:18.133
And regardless of how you feel

00:11:18.133 --> 00:11:20.200
about the ethics of
kicking politicians off Twitter,

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.834
it's just a huge quality
of life improvement.

00:11:22.834 --> 00:11:24.300
Like when Trump
got kicked off Twitter,

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.234
trying to live in a world where
people like Trump and Greene

00:11:26.234 --> 00:11:27.567
are constantly
screaming and saying

00:11:27.567 --> 00:11:29.434
[bleep] Twitter is like trying
to have a conversation

00:11:29.434 --> 00:11:32.567
with a friend on the street
next to a jackhammer.

00:11:32.567 --> 00:11:35.234
Wow, it's great to see you!
[ Jackhammer hammering ]

00:11:35.234 --> 00:11:36.200
I said it's great to see you!

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.567
Ma, this jackhammer!

00:11:37.567 --> 00:11:40.234
Freaking de Blasio, am I right?!
[ Laughter ]

00:11:40.234 --> 00:11:42.801
What? Oh, yeah, I forgot!

00:11:42.801 --> 00:11:45.567
Freaking Adams, am I right?!
[ Hammering stops ]

00:11:45.567 --> 00:11:48.200
People are so deeply invested
in the unhinged idea

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.601
that any attempt at all
to curb the spread of COVID

00:11:50.601 --> 00:11:51.868
is somehow tyranny.

00:11:51.868 --> 00:11:54.234
For example,
Congressman Madison Cawthorn

00:11:54.234 --> 00:11:56.133
tweeted over the weekend
"Our Founding Fathers

00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:58.300
wouldn't recognize
the America we live in today.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.167
They would be horrified,
and rightly so."

00:12:00.167 --> 00:12:02.234
I mean, no one
from the 1700s

00:12:02.234 --> 00:12:04.434
would recognize anything.

00:12:04.434 --> 00:12:06.467
I mean, Thomas Jefferson
was a renowned inventor,

00:12:06.467 --> 00:12:10.767
but he'd still [bleep] his pants
if you showed him a Roomba.

00:12:10.767 --> 00:12:13.067
On the other hand, if you want
to invoke the founding fathers,

00:12:13.067 --> 00:12:16.167
George Washington famously
ordered his troops

00:12:16.167 --> 00:12:17.801
to get inoculated
against smallpox.

00:12:17.801 --> 00:12:19.434
And if you refused,

00:12:19.434 --> 00:12:22.133
General Washington would
famously say...

00:12:22.133 --> 00:12:25.534
-Sayonara, sucka.

00:12:25.534 --> 00:12:27.033
-And yet,
despite their obsession

00:12:27.033 --> 00:12:29.200
with prioritizing these
treatments over vaccines,

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.834
they can't even seem
to get the names right,

00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:33.634
as Fox host Brian Kilmeade
recently demonstrated.

00:12:33.634 --> 00:12:36.100
-Aaron Rodgers is saying
what we've been saying.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.968
You especially, Carley,
yesterday,

00:12:37.968 --> 00:12:40.267
where the therapeutics
of that mano --

00:12:40.267 --> 00:12:42.534
monocolonial, uh,
the treatment --

00:12:42.534 --> 00:12:44.868
-Monoclonal antibodies, yeah.
-Yeah, antibodies.

00:12:44.868 --> 00:12:46.901
-Yeah, monocolonial.

00:12:46.901 --> 00:12:48.534
You know the thing
Mr. Peanut wears.

00:12:48.534 --> 00:12:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:12:50.701 --> 00:12:53.267
It's almost like they're not
monomaniacally monopolizing

00:12:53.267 --> 00:12:55.100
the monologue
about monoclonal molecules,

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.000
and that was today's joke
for your SAT prep course,

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.267
[ Chime plays ]

00:12:59.267 --> 00:13:00.868
Study up, kids, or don't.

00:13:00.868 --> 00:13:02.701
It's your future.
I don't care.

00:13:02.701 --> 00:13:05.467
Anyway, Brian, do you know
any preparation at all

00:13:05.467 --> 00:13:07.133
before you go on TV,
or do they just pull you

00:13:07.133 --> 00:13:09.100
out of bed,
dump cold water in your face

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.901
and throw it in front
of the camera like a hostage?

00:13:10.901 --> 00:13:13.868
"Oh, God. Where am I?
Why are the lights so bright?"

00:13:13.868 --> 00:13:15.400
"Just read the card, Yankee!"

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.133
"Monocolonial antibodies."

00:13:17.133 --> 00:13:19.300
[ Laughter ]

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.968
2022 is arriving
with a fresh set of challenges,

00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:24.133
along with the ones we were
already facing,

00:13:24.133 --> 00:13:26.968
and the time is now to band
together in solidarity

00:13:26.968 --> 00:13:29.100
and do something about them,
whether it's saving democracy

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.567
or keeping people healthy
and safe

00:13:30.567 --> 00:13:32.534
from a highly contagious
respiratory virus.

00:13:32.534 --> 00:13:35.400
We should be working together
to solve these problems.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.634
We can do it.

00:13:36.634 --> 00:13:39.467
To quote the song,
imagine all the people

00:13:39.467 --> 00:13:40.734
living life in peace.

00:13:40.734 --> 00:13:42.501
-...you!

00:13:42.501 --> 00:13:45.000
[ Laughter ]

00:13:47.267 --> 00:13:48.634
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:48.634 --> 00:13:52.167
♪♪

00:13:52.167 --> 00:13:53.834
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings over

00:13:53.834 --> 00:13:55.868
two million meals a year
to men, women and children

00:13:55.868 --> 00:13:58.400
living with HIV, AIDS, cancer
and other serious illnesses

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.367
and need your help
now more than ever.

00:14:00.367 --> 00:14:02.367
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:14:02.367 --> 00:14:04.667
Stay safe, get vaccinated.
We love you.

